; TinyTronscroll in a window on Linux (SDL): ../TinyTronscroll.ml, the
; same text, linked with the platform that has a window
; (lib_playground/platforms/sdl), for a game against another window,
; another computer, or a board that runs mini-9pi. Dune's alone: SDL
; is outside what mini-ml compiles.
;   dune exec games/arcade/sdl/TinyTronscroll.exe                        (two on one keyboard)
;   dune exec games/arcade/sdl/TinyTronscroll.exe -- net=host bind=0.0.0.0
;   dune exec games/arcade/sdl/TinyTronscroll.exe -- net=join host=192.168.9.1
; (against mini-ml's program on a board the game plays and says DESYNC:
; a checksum is Marshal's bytes, the same by one compiler only.
; Multiplayer.mli)
(copy_files ../TinyTronscroll.ml)
(executable
 (name TinyTronscroll)
 (flags (:standard -w -32-37-69))
 (libraries ix_playground ix_playground_sdl ix_core caps unix))
